4. Architecture Principle – Reuse Existing Tables

John emphasized the project’s primary architectural principle:

Always extend existing tables before creating new ones.

If a feature shares approximately 70–80% of the functionality of an existing module:

* Extend the existing table.
* Avoid duplicate entities.

Objective

Maintain:

* Common database structure
* Shared business logic
* Shared UI components
* Shared APIs

This supports the long-term monorepo strategy.

