8. Knowledge Base Permissioning

Knowledge Base permissioning was identified as a high-priority feature.

Permission Hierarchy

Knowledge Base
        ↓
Hierarchy Node
        ↓
Knowledge Article

Permissions should support inheritance while allowing overrides at each level.

⸻

Permission Assignment

Users should be assignable directly from the relevant UI.

Examples:

Knowledge Base

Assign:

* Stefan → Editor

All child nodes inherit.

⸻

Hierarchy Node

Assign:

* Sean → Editor

Child articles inherit.

⸻

Knowledge Article

Assign:

* Stefan → Author
* John → Reviewer

Only that article receives the assignment.

⸻

Permission Types

Support configurable permissions including:

* View
* Create
* Edit
* Delete
* Publish
* Archive

⸻

Technical Design

Introduce a junction table relating:

* Users
* Knowledge Bases
* Hierarchy Nodes
* Knowledge Articles

to support record-level permission management.

⸻

9. UI Expectations

Permission management should be performed directly from:

* Knowledge Base pages
* Hierarchy Node pages
* Knowledge Article pages

instead of only from a centralized administration page.

